Betfred may close 73 more betting shops, blaming higher machine gaming duty

Betfred has started consulting staff on the possible closure of 73 shops, putting 365 jobs at risk, iGaming Business reports. CEO Jo Whittaker pointed to successive tax rises and higher employment costs, including the increase in Machine Games Duty from 20% to 25% announced in the autumn budget, with the new rate starting in April 2027. Betfred closed 132 shops in August and had 1,094 before this review, down from 1,680 in 2017. It estimates each shop pays about £32,000 a year to racing through media rights and the levy. The consultation does not mean all 73 will close.

